  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Landscape Analysis Aquaculture MKD Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mekong River Delta is ranked as the world&apos;s third largest delta, rich in biodiversity and plays a vital role in Vietnam&apos;s agricultural landscape.The local aquaculture sector, especially in brackish and freshwater aquaculture, is of paramount importance. Favourable environmental conditions, and abundant fishery resources, make it a priority area for collaboration between Vietnam and the Netherlands. However, its vulnerability to climate change poses a significant threat to the lives and livelihoods of its inhabitants.The purpose of this project is to analyse and map the aquaculture landscape in the Mekong River Delta in Vietnam in relation to private sector development and business opportunities for Dutch companies.To get a comprehensive understanding of the specific stakeholders, conditions, threats and dynamics influencing the aquaculture sector, a context-analysis is needed. The analysis serves as a foundation for informed decision-making, strategic planning, and effective resource allocation, ensuring that future efforts align with the local context and opportunities for Dutch businesses.</narrative>
  </description>
